  "title": "Formal Correspondence: Drafting a Complaint",
  "topic": "Writing a formal complaint regarding a late delivery (CEFR B2)",
  "body": "<h3>Exercise: Professional Complaint Letter</h3><p>You are a Procurement Manager at a logistics firm. You ordered a shipment of specialized hardware from a supplier, 'Global Tech Solutions', which was guaranteed for delivery by the 1st of the month. It is now the 10th, and the shipment has not arrived, causing delays in your production schedule.</p><p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a formal letter of complaint (150–200 words). Your letter must include the following points:</p><ul><li>A clear reference to the order number and date.</li><li>A professional explanation of the inconvenience caused by the delay.</li><li>A firm request for an immediate status update and a proposed solution (e.g., expedited shipping or a discount).</li><li>A professional closing statement.</li></ul><p><em>Pedagogical Hint: Avoid emotional language. Use the passive voice to maintain a professional distance (e.g., 'It has come to my attention that...' instead of 'I saw that...'). / Vermeiden Sie emotionale Sprache; nutzen Sie das Passiv für eine professionelle Distanz.</em></p>"
}
